Copyright status of "A Source Book in Physics"
==============================================

Work:       A Source Book in Physics (Source Books in the History of the
            Sciences), ed. William Francis Magie.
            First published 1935 (McGraw-Hill; copyright registration
            A82952, 3 May 1935). Later issued by Harvard University Press.
Edition:    Eighth Printing, Harvard University Press, 1963.
            Notice in the book: "Original edition copyright 1935, 1963 by
            the President and Fellows of Harvard College."

This file records the copyright status of the source material only. It is
not legal advice. Status was checked in 2026; it was not reviewed by a
lawyer.


People
------

William Francis Magie (editor and author of the editorial text)
  Died:       1943.
  EU term:    Life + 70 years. Expired 31 December 2013. In the public
              domain in the EU, Switzerland and other life+70 countries.

Gregory D. Walcott (General Editor of the series; author of the
"General Editor's Preface")
  Died:       1959 (per Wikipedia; no exact date known).
  EU term:    Life + 70 years. Expires 31 December 2029. The General
              Editor's Preface is protected in the EU until then and
              enters the public domain on 1 January 2030.


United States
-------------

Renewal:      Filed. Catalog of Copyright Entries, Renewal Registrations,
              January-June 1962:
                MAGIE, WILLIAM FRANCIS. A source book in physics.
                (c) 3May35; A82952. Angelina MacLaren (NK); 11May62;
                R295235.
Renewal by:   Angelina MacLaren, as next of kin (NK) of the author.
              The renewal was not filed by Harvard. The "1963" in the
              Harvard notice is not a renewal date; no 1963 renewal
              entry exists for this work (checked: Books renewals,
              January-June and July-December 1963).
Term:         95 years from first publication, 1935 + 95. Protected
              until 31 December 2030. Public domain from 1 January 2031.


Other material
--------------

The book is an anthology of extracts from many authors, mostly published
before 1900. Each extract, and any translation or editorial matter by a
person other than Magie or Walcott, has its own term, which was not
individually reviewed. Translations made for this book are the main open
question.


Digital edition
---------------

The Typst transcription, the figure sources and the build files in this
repository are a digital reproduction of the work above. This file does
not grant any licence to the work itself in countries where it is still
protected. No licence has been chosen for the transcription or figures
themselves.


